        "fire",
        "poison",
        "primal"
      ],
      "description": "<p>Toxic materials and churning rubbish within the filth fire's body explode in one of three ways. The filth fire chooses the effect, but it can't make the same choice twice in a row.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fiery Beam</strong> (evocation, fire, primal) The filth fire expels a 30ft Line of flame that deals 3d6 Fire Damage damage with a Basic DC 21 Reflex Saving Throw save.</li>\n<li><strong>Shrapnel Blast</strong> (evocation, primal) The filth fire shoots jagged rubbish out in a 5ft Emanation that deals 2d12 Piercing Damage damage with a Basic DC 21 Reflex Saving Throw save.</li>\n<li><strong>Toxic Fumes</strong> (evocation, poison, primal) The filth fire belches a 15ft Cone of toxic smoke that deals 2d6 Poison Damage damage (Basic DC 21 Fortitude Saving Throw save). A creature that fails is also Sickened 1 (or Sickened 2 on a critical failure).</li>\n</ul>",
